    <DataNode elementId="AT4G37150-MONOMER" textLabel="Methylesterase 9" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O23171" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="1200" centerY="715" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">This enzyme has methylesterase activity against methyl indole-3-acetate (MeIAA), methyl salicylate (MeSA), and methyl jasmonate (MeJA) &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; but its biological activity &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; has not been conclusively determined |CITS: [18467465]|. MES9 has higher activity with MeSA than MeIAA or MeJA &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt;. In addition, it can complement the systemic acquired resistance (SAR)-deficient phenotype of tobacco plants with reduced SABP2 expression. And, its transcript levels are up-regulated in response to pathogen attack. All of these suggest that MES9 likely plays a role in SA metabolism and SAR responses &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [18643994]|.</Comment>
