    <DataNode elementId="AT3G10870-MONOMER" textLabel="methyl indole-3-acetate methyltransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SG92" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="1200" centerY="955" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">MES17, one of several carboxylesterases identified in Arabidopsis, can hydrolyze methyl indole-3-acetate (MeIAA) to release free IAA, an important phytohormone |CITS: [18467465]|. It shows substrate specificity &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt;, and, unlike several other methylesterase family members, it does not have the ability to act on methyl jamsonate, methyl salicylate, or methyl gibberellates |CITS: [18467465]|. A recombinant form of the enzyme purified from &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; has a K&lt;sub&gt;cat&lt;/sub&gt; value of 0.18 s&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; when measured using MeIAA at a pH of 7.5. The activity of this enzyme can be strongly inhibited (44%-75%) by 5 mM Fe&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;, Fe&lt;sup&gt;3+&lt;/sup&gt;, Cu&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;, Zn &lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;, whereas 5 mM Ca&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt; and Mn &lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt; only cause a mild reduction in enzyme activity. MES17 hydrolase activity is not affected by 5 mM Na&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt;, Mg&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;, K&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt;, or NH&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt; |CITS: [18467465]|. Several other methylesterases in Arabidopsis, namely MES1, MES2, MES3, MES7, MES9, MES16, and MES18 can cleave MeIAA &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; but their &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; role in MeIAA catabolism has not been confirmed |CITS: [18467465]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G10870-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT3G10870.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9SG92" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="MeIAA methylesterase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="methyl indole-3-acetic acid methylesterase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="IAA methylesterase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_4" value="indole-3-acetic acid methylesterase" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33796, RXN-16751, RXN-0A-16751" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="3" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G10870.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT3G10870" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_18467465" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT2G23560-MONOMER" textLabel="Methylesterase 7" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O80472" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="1035" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">This enzyme has methylesterase activity against methyl indole-3-acetate (MeIAA) and methyl salicylate (MeSA) &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; but its biological activity &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; has not been determined |CITS: [18467465]|. Transcript levels for this gene are up-regulated following pathogen attack |CITS: [18467465]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G23560-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G23560.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O80472" />
